.TH XIL\-SETUP "1" "2026\-10\-08" "xil\-pipeline 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xil\-setup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xil\-setup
[-h] [--device {auto,cuda,cpu}] [--cuda-index TAG] [--dir PATH] [--python VER] [--force] [--dry-run] {chatterbox,whisper,mmaudio}
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create and verify the virtual environment a local ML worker runs under. 'chatterbox' builds venv\-chatterbox (PyTorch + chatterbox\-tts) for local TTS; 'whisper' builds venv\-whisper (faster\-whisper) for xil stem\-verify; 'mmaudio' clones MMAudio and builds venv\-mmaudio for local SFX. PyTorch comes as CUDA wheels when an NVIDIA GPU is found, CPU wheels otherwise.

.TP
\fB{chatterbox,whisper,mmaudio}\fR
what to set up

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fI\,{auto,cuda,cpu}\/\fR
PyTorch build to install (auto: CUDA if nvidia\-smi works, else CPU)

.TP
\fB\-\-cuda\-index\fR \fI\,TAG\/\fR
PyTorch CUDA wheel index tag

.TP
\fB\-\-dir\fR \fI\,PATH\/\fR
directory to create the venv in

.TP
\fB\-\-python\fR \fI\,VER\/\fR
Python version for the venv (default: 3.13; 3.12 for mmaudio)

.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
delete and rebuild an existing venv

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
print the commands without running them

.SH COMMENTS
The venv is created in \-\-dir, else $XIL_CODEROOT, else the workspace root: the
places the xil commands look for it. Uses uv when it is on PATH, otherwise
python \-m venv and pip. Running it again on a working venv does nothing.

